    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A frontier march east of the Elbe founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> in 1157, whose ruler became one of the seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#prince-elector">electors</a> of the Empire.</li><li>From 1415 the Hohenzollerns ruled it, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1618 and building a standing army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">the Great Elector</a>.</li><li>In 1701 its elector became King in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> remained the Prussian heartland until the Empire ended in 1806.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> had an African colony: from 1683 its fort of Gross Friedrichsburg stood on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> in today’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ghana">Ghana</a>, until the Prussian king sold it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#dutch">Dutch</a> in 1717.</p></aside>
    </section>

